  "drawn_by": "evalgen.splits.draw_split(items, tune_every=3)",
  "purpose": "The development slice and locked holdout that prompts/manifest.json's phase_two_protocol requires for model-specific prompt tuning. Tune on `tune`; evaluate ONCE on `holdout`.",
  "rules": [
    "Deterministic traversal, no seed: blocks ordered by (stratum, item id), every third block to the tune slice.",
    "A long_context dilation never leaves its base item's side. RET-101..112 are 3x and 10x dilations of six earlier items -- the same transcript at three lengths -- so splitting a block would measure a tuned prompt on a copy of what it was tuned on.",
    "Dilation blocks form their own stratum, because a block spans two families by construction and striping it inside the base's family decides long_context's balance as a side effect."
  ],
  "contamination": "THIS HOLDOUT IS FRESH-EYES AT BEST, NOT CLEAN. Every item ships an `expected_failure` string naming the exact wrong answer a model gives, and EXPERIMENTS.md:401 records that the phase-one items were already used to select the v9_16_e1 prompt edits. Any figure measured here is an UPPER BOUND and must be reported as one.",
